# Line endings.
#
# The repository is developed on Windows (`core.autocrlf=true`) and built into a
# Linux container. That combination has one classic failure: a shell script
# committed with CRLF is checked out inside the image with CRLF, and the kernel
# then reads the shebang as `/bin/sh\r` and reports
#
#     exec /app/backend/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which names a file that is plainly present. Pinning the entrypoint - and
# anything else the container executes or parses - to LF removes the dependency
# on whatever `core.autocrlf` happens to be set to on the machine that commits.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Model artifacts and other binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.joblib binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
